 C_2=\widetilde\chi C[A_1]=C[V_1]. \tag{3.7}
\end{equation}$$ When $t_0>0$ the cutoff and all of its derivatives vanish at $t_0$. The products therefore extend smoothly by zero to the earlier times, where the seed need not be defined. Multiplication by a time cutoff preserves the spatial divergence cancellation. Its derivative along the parent flow contributes the term $$\begin{equation}
 R_{\widetilde\chi}=\widetilde\chi'\,(A_1+C[A_1]) \tag{3.8}
\end{equation}$$ to the residual, so the cutoff error depends on the size of the wave while it is being switched on.

