**Proposition 5.1.** There is an absolute exponent $C$ such that each coefficient $c$ among $$(D_aX)^{\pm1},\qquad M,\qquad
 \kappa/\lambda,\qquad \lambda^2/|\kappa|^2,\qquad P_\kappa$$ satisfies (D.6). Let $f(t,x)$ be a field with values in a normed space such that $|f|_m\le C_m'A_f\mathsf D^m$ for every $m\ge0$ and a number $A_f$. Then $$\begin{equation}
